<!doctype html>
<html>
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8">
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no">
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/materialize/1.0.0/css/materialize.min.css">
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/icon?family=Material+Icons" rel="stylesheet">
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="/js/dark.css">
		<style>
			.icon-btn {
				display: inline-flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				width: 30px;
				height: 30px;
				border-radius: 50%;
				border: 1px solid #fff;
				color: #fff;
				text-decoration: none;
				cursor: pointer;
			}
			.icon-btn.icon-btn-delete {
				background: #d32f2f;
				border-color: #d32f2f;
				color: #000;
			}
			.confidence-high {
				color: #4caf50;
			}
			.confidence-low {
				color: #ffb74d;
			}
		</style>
        <title>{{.Page.Title}} - Admin</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		{{template "navbar.tmpl" .}}
		<div class="container">
            <h4>Duplicates Detected <span style="font-size:0.6em;opacity:0.7;">(Experimental)</span></h4>
            <p>Maps under 20 grids flagged as likely spawn zones, dungeon
                instances, house interiors, or other generated/orphaned
                layers. Nothing here is deleted automatically -- review each
                one and delete it directly from this page, or leave it
                alone. This detector is new and still being tuned; expect
                some legitimate small maps to show up here too, especially
                in the lower-confidence section below.</p>

            <h5><span class="confidence-high">&#9679;</span> Player structure -- no minimap ever rendered</h5>
            <p>Maps that are 100.000% black on every single tile, with zero
                exceptions. Real houses and stonesteads have no in-game
                minimap at all, so this is the strongest signal in this
                report -- there is nothing on these layers to lose.</p>
            {{if not .InteriorsNoRender}}
            <p><i>None found.</i></p>
            {{else}}
            {{template "admin/duplicates.tmpl:maptable" .InteriorsNoRender}}
            {{end}}

            <h5><span class="confidence-high">&#9679;</span> Dungeon/basement instance -- partial minimap content</h5>
            <p>Maps that are almost entirely black like the group above, but
                at least one tile has a sliver of real rendered content
                (a corridor or wall line) -- consistent with a real dungeon
                or basement instance rather than a player structure. Not
                sorted by which specific instance template each one is (real
                interior content is too sparse per-tile for that yet) --
                every one lands in this bucket for review, worth a closer
                look before deleting since there's actual explored content
                here.</p>
            {{if not .InteriorsPartial}}
            <p><i>None found.</i></p>
            {{else}}
            {{template "admin/duplicates.tmpl:maptable" .InteriorsPartial}}
            {{end}}

            <h5><span class="confidence-high">&#9679;</span> High confidence -- shared layout, no entrance marker</h5>
            <p>Maps that both match at least {{.ThresholdPct}}% of another map's tile
                layout <i>and</i> have no Mineshaft/Cave marker on them --
                every confirmed spawn zone found in testing hit both signals
                at once.</p>
            {{$anyHighConfidence := false}}
            {{range .Groups}}{{if .NoneHaveEntry}}{{$anyHighConfidence = true}}{{end}}{{end}}
            {{if not $anyHighConfidence}}
            <p><i>None found.</i></p>
            {{end}}
            {{range .Groups}}
            {{if .NoneHaveEntry}}
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-content">
                    <h5>{{len .Maps}} maps, ~{{.GridCount}} grids each</h5>
                    {{template "admin/duplicates.tmpl:maptable" .Maps}}
                </div>
            </div>
            {{end}}
            {{end}}

            <h5><span class="confidence-low">&#9679;</span> Lower confidence -- shared layout only</h5>
            <p>Maps that match at least {{.ThresholdPct}}% of another map's layout but do
                have an entrance marker on them -- less likely to be junk,
                but still worth a look since a real map shouldn't normally
                duplicate another one's tiles.</p>
            {{$anyLowConfidence := false}}
            {{range .Groups}}{{if not .NoneHaveEntry}}{{$anyLowConfidence = true}}{{end}}{{end}}
            {{if not $anyLowConfidence}}
            <p><i>None found.</i></p>
            {{end}}
            {{range .Groups}}
            {{if not .NoneHaveEntry}}
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-content">
                    <h5>{{len .Maps}} maps, ~{{.GridCount}} grids each</h5>
                    {{template "admin/duplicates.tmpl:maptable" .Maps}}
                </div>
            </div>
            {{end}}
            {{end}}

            <h5><span class="confidence-low">&#9679;</span> Lower confidence -- no entrance marker, no layout match</h5>
            <p>Small maps with no entrance marker that don't match any other
                map's layout. In testing this caught real spawn zones, but
                also real dungeons/caves whose entrance marker simply never
                got uploaded (an older client, or icons not yet enabled) --
                check each one before deleting.</p>
            {{if not .Solo}}
            <p><i>None found.</i></p>
            {{else}}
            {{template "admin/duplicates.tmpl:maptable" .Solo}}
            {{end}}
		</div>
        <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/materialize/1.0.0/js/materialize.min.js"></script>
        <script>M.AutoInit();</script>
	</body>
</html>

{{define "admin/duplicates.tmpl:maptable"}}
<form method="POST" action="/admin/deleteMaps" onsubmit="var n=this.querySelectorAll('input[name=map]:checked').length; if(n===0){alert('Select at least one map first.'); return false;} return confirm('Delete '+n+' selected map(s)? This removes every grid, tile, marker, road, and custom marker on each one. THIS CANNOT BE UNDONE.');">
<input type="hidden" name="redirect" value="/admin/duplicateMaps">
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th><label><input type="checkbox" title="Select all" onclick="this.closest('table').querySelectorAll('input[name=map]').forEach(cb=>cb.checked=this.checked)"/><span></span></label></th>
            <th>ID</th>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Actions</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {{range .}}
        <tr>
            <td><label><input type="checkbox" name="map" value="{{.ID}}"/><span></span></label></td>
            <td>{{.ID}}</td>
            <td>{{.Name}}</td>
            <td>
                <div class="icon-btn-group" style="display:flex;gap:4px;">
                    <a href="/admin/map?map={{.ID}}" class="icon-btn" title="Edit"><i class="material-icons">edit</i></a>
                    <a href="#previewMap-{{.ID}}" class="icon-btn modal-trigger" title="Preview stitched image"><i class="material-icons">image</i></a>
                    <a href="#deleteMap-{{.ID}}" class="icon-btn icon-btn-delete modal-trigger" title="Delete"><i class="material-icons">close</i></a>
                </div>
                <div id="previewMap-{{.ID}}" class="modal">
                    <div class="modal-content">
                        <h4>Preview -- "{{.Name}}"</h4>
                        <img src="/admin/mapPreview?map={{.ID}}" style="max-width:100%;image-rendering:pixelated;border:1px solid #444;">
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal-footer">
                        <a href="#!" class="modal-close waves-effect waves-light green btn">Close</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div id="deleteMap-{{.ID}}" class="modal">
                    <div class="modal-content">
                        <h4>Delete "{{.Name}}"</h4>
                        <p>This will remove every grid, tile, marker, road, and custom marker on this map layer.</p>
                        <h5>THIS CANNOT BE UNDONE!</h5>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal-footer">
                        <a href="#!" class="modal-close waves-effect waves-light green btn">Cancel</a>
                        <a href="/admin/deleteMap?map={{.ID}}&redirect=/admin/duplicateMaps" class="waves-effect waves-light red btn">DELETE</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
    </tbody>
</table>
<button type="submit" class="waves-effect waves-light red btn" style="margin: 8px 0 16px;">Delete Selected</button>
</form>
{{end}}
